{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/529362-coverting-nightbane-to-nwod","id":529362,"title":"Coverting Nightbane to nWoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-26T15:56:16-07:00","id":529362,"title":"Coverting Nightbane to nWoD","content":"I was wanting to try this out. The Storyteller system is so much more mechanically sound than the Palladium system. I was wondering who here has tried to do it and what their success was at it. Also, if they did do it, any tips?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T17:08:13-07:00","id":529414,"title":"","content":"I want my motorcycle body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T21:09:21-07:00","id":529578,"title":"","content":"Never tried it, sorry, although I am curious about the intent here.<br /> <br /> Do you simply want a mechanical conversion, or are you picturing epic magic battles between nightlord avatars and mages, while a black ops squad of nightbane and forsaken commits a surgical strike?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T05:31:02-07:00","id":529810,"title":"","content":"A mechanical conversion is what I would like. You see, I used Nightbane + Beyond the Supernatural + Ninjas and Superspies + Mystic China + TMNT for a rather epic tabletop game. However, the group I am with now have not had a very broad experience with gaming. They much prefer the Storyteller system and, to me, it is easier and faster overall. Especially in terms of combat and growth. The Palladium system is clunky and has too many loopholes. I was hoping to bring the flavor of Nightbane to the Storyteller system so that my new players can experience the awesomeness that was in the old game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T05:45:46-07:00","id":529820,"title":"","content":"I've given it some thought before, but mostly back in CWoD where it would be a LOT harder to convert. Off the top of my head, I don't see any reason it wouldn't be an easy switch. My suggests are to take a look at the WtF rules or Shapeshifters regarding, well, the Shapeshifting aspect of the game. I would make the Nightbane powers similar to some of the Hunter stuff, more like Merits than Powers really. My last thought, off the top of my head, is to not convert everything, just the stuff for the players because you seem like a Palladium Vet so you should be able to convert enemies on the fly. Just my two cents. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T05:59:44-07:00","id":529828,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I have been playing Palladoum games and converting some of the stuff. I was thinking a point buy system for the Morphus for the Nightbane themselves. I was also thinking of uing the Dread Powers from Hunter to mimic a great deal of things. The nWoD has enough things to go &quot;This now applies to this splat.&quot; But the big sticking point is...what about mages and psychics? Just use some of the Merits and Dread Powers or should I use MtAw stuff for the mages in Nightbane?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T15:39:37-07:00","id":530367,"title":"","content":"Well, you can just use the Morphus tables straight up; as far as I can remember, there aren't any mechanics connected to the results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T18:19:54-07:00","id":530474,"title":"","content":"Actually, there are mechanical benefits to all of them. Most of the time, it is just adding to the Horror Factor, but a lot of them, like the whole &quot;I have tiger fangs and tentacles made of metal coming from my back while the lower half of me is that of a motorcycle&quot; can give you tons of mechanical bennies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T19:26:44-07:00","id":530514,"title":"","content":"Shows on me for just looking at the pretty tables someone tossed up <a href=\"http://rpgaming.prophpbb.com/topic4703.html\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> I am a sham.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-27T23:56:22-07:00","id":530721,"title":"","content":"Have you looked at the Demon game? It has many similar elements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T02:18:00-07:00","id":530773,"title":"","content":"@amechra It's ok. Stuff happens.<br /> @Diggs Thanks for the tip. I had forgotten about their &quot;Pick one of these and a couple of these&quot; method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T18:14:48-07:00","id":531470,"title":"","content":"I was also referring to the players having a human form and a monster form they can change into, as well as being hunted by a more numerous enemy that more or less runs the world. The games have similar themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T18:29:31-07:00","id":531480,"title":"","content":"I understood you meant both. I love DtD and enjoy the themes of it. Although, with DtD, you can never actually strike back fully against the main enemy of the setting whereas in Nightbane, you do have a shot at killing one of the Night Lords.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-28T21:22:00-07:00","id":531703,"title":"","content":"You can knock out a piece of the God Machine. Obviously, there are some differences. You could switch out the God Machine for a group of angels (archangels) or have them act as the face of the God Machine. I think you could hack Demon to recreate the major players. I would have to look at Nightbane again to see what else it has unless you want to bring up what elements exactly you want to find in ST.<br /> <br /> I can't find my Nightbane book, but I found the supplements, go figure. Demon for Nightbane, Armory and Hurt Locker for Mystic China, Mage for astral, Changeling has dream stuff, Hunter covers the human agents and is probably best bet for antagonist creation, GMC/Core2 for psychics, I'm at a loss for TMNT and I actually never looked at Beyond the Supernatural, but it seemed more like a Hunter game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","user":"Diggs","date":". 05-29-2015, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T03:15:28-07:00","id":531826,"title":"","content":"Well, for the martial art side of things, I was thinking of nerfing the old Street Fighter RPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-29T18:59:20-07:00","id":532641,"title":"","content":"I have no clue how well that might work with NWOD 2.0","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T18:01:27-07:00","id":858642,"title":"","content":"I agree. I'm curious as to how thsi would work out. I'd honestly like to see some classes from RIFTS set up to work in nWoD and CofD. Cyberknights for instance would be a spiffy Conspiracy. But so could other Nightbane RCC's as well. I also agree that Demon would be a good start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11556-coyoteschosen","name":"CoyotesChosen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-03T18:11:07-07:00","id":858650,"title":"","content":"......been a while since people posted in this thread...that being said, while its not Storyteller there IS a RIFTS to Savage World conversion happening at the moment (sanctioned by Kevin even). I've not played that system but its probably a lot more mechanically sound than Palladium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11535-furoan","name":"Furoan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"52"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T05:23:54-08:00","id":1270088,"title":"","content":"Recently picked up the new Nightbane book and once again came back to this idea. I actually don't think it would be too hard anymore. It would be a simple conversion of stats that would be the largest challenge, but, again, this would be only time consuming. I would build it from the ground up. I think there are some similar themes with Beast now. Not mechanically, just ideas of alternate worlds and hidden enemies. I think I may take the time to write something general. That could be applied across the board. Unless someone has found a good conversion in the years since this? If not, and there's still an interest, I'll post what I have later. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Cheers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T14:34:26-07:00","id":1552674,"title":"","content":"I havent logged in here for a ... a good bit of time. lol. But Im back as Im running games again. Saw this in My inbox and started thinking about it. Frankly, this wouldnt be AS diffiicult as it used to be. IMHO, the easiest way would be to use DtR for most stuff, and other splats to for references. I actually am thinking about doing very similar for a version of CthulhuTech the same way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11556-coyoteschosen","name":"CoyotesChosen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11556_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}